      ],
      "detail": "Box probability is normalized by actual reciprocal-density integrals; its x,y,1/z,x/z,y/z moments are derived. The true ordered prism has its separately derived probability and max/min moments. Raw x/y/max means scale by D, raw inverse-z mean by 1/D, so arguments are dimensionless. Restored density includes factor4; symmetric charged mass is the true ordered-half mass. None of these facts is assumed as a supplied mass or moment certificate."
    },
    {
