      "status": "PASS_NARROW_SOURCE",
      "evidence": [
        "JensenBounds:64-67,83-188,207-286",
        "ActualThirdOriginalBoxMoments:26-115",
        "Mathlib.Analysis.Convex.Integral:199-211"
      ],
      "detail": "NEW uses concavity on [2,infinity): E f(new) <= f(E new), with new>=2 from the original full corner test. OLD uses a lower chord, then is subtracted. The original no-crossing guard plus oldHigh>2 forces oldLow>=2. oldHigh<=2, including equality, is handled by OLD nonnegativity. Concavity across the clamping point2 is never asserted."
    },
    {
      "id": "symmetric_historical_kernel",
      "status": "PASS_NARROW_SOURCE",
      "evidence": [
        "JensenBounds:116-188",
        "ActualThirdOriginalP4ASymmetricPairRealRescue:238-291",
        "ActualThirdOriginalP4ASymmetricTentPrerequisites:80-151",
        "ActualThirdOriginalP4ASymmetricBLeaf:44-127"
      ],
      "detail": "Below mu, the exact source square chord is the average of two genuine ordered minorant chords with common endpoints; this allows either sign of fh-fl and retains the selected label. B uses its actual equal-coefficient mean. Above mu, the actual ordered max coordinate mean 2*(b*log(b/a)-b+a)/log(b/a)^2 is used. No false symmetry of the raw historical cap/kernel or independence of ordered x/y is assumed."
    },
    {
      "id": "literal_Q80_operations_and_endpoints",
      "status": "PASS_NARROW_SOURCE",
