        "Arithmetic:point_constructor_source,mul_source,floor_rounds_down,ceiling_rounds_up",
        "P2HistoricI80DivisionSoundness:25-29,60-83"
      ],
      "detail": "The max12 mesh16384 point queries and original log32 arithmetic are used. Exact raw rational endpoints retain num/den queries. Every mean operation, historical four-corner signed division, clipped weight, signed endpoint difference, lower chord floor and final max0 is preserved. Exact multiplication commutativity proves Python __rmul__ operand-order identities including outward roundings; it is not merely an enclosure replacement. No P112/P160 query or alternate endpoint is used."
    },
    {
      "id": "internal_guards_derived",
      "status": "PASS_NARROW_SOURCE",
      "evidence": [
        "JensenSelection:145-234",
        "JensenBounds:35-62",
        "Parent LogGuards:uniform lower-log and squared-log proofs"
